{"name":"King’s Cloak","hex":"#c48692","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"},{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak","wikidata":"Q516992"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloak.jpg/500px-Cloak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloak.jpg/500px-Cloak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cloak, 1580–1600 Victoria and Albert Museum, No. 793-1901","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACloak.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Moctezuma_Xocoyotzin.png/500px-Moctezuma_Xocoyotzin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Moctezuma_Xocoyotzin.png/500px-Moctezuma_Xocoyotzin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aztec emperor Moctezuma II wearing a tilmàtli","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoctezuma_Xocoyotzin.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg/500px-Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg/1280px-Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg/500px-Couple_cloak_Louvre_G99.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Couple hiding under the same cloak, fragment of an Ancient Greek red-figure cup, c. 525–500 BC, found in Athens. Louvre Museum